    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project's test suite contains the single `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system, keeping structural impact low by working through small, cohesive units.\n\n**Changes (4 files):**\n\n1. **`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 split into two tiny static methods:\n   - `points(Owner)` sums owner-only factors: +2 email, +1 namesake 0, +3 tenure > 365 days.\n   - `level(int points)` buckets a total into 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping and repointed `membershipLevel` to `level(points(owner))`.\n\n3. **`HouseholdTier.java`** \u2014 the household factor now adds +2 points (household of 3+) and recomputes the level, instead of forcing level 3. Its signature is unchanged, so the two responder classes needed no edits.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field (drives the generated DTO's getter/setter) and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/max to reflect the new derivation.\n\nBoth fields are now returned. The household factor stays in `HouseholdTier` where the repository is available; owner-only factors stay in the mapper \u2014 so no single method or class grew, and the responder pipeline classes were left untouched.",
