    "probe_recall": 0.5609756097560976,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes. I've split each step into what it **validates** (can reject the request) versus what **side-effect** it applies.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n**0. Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The whole endpoint requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 its escalation handler.\n\n## Steps, in execution order\n\n1. **RequireOwnerFields** \u2014 *validation.* Reads the `@RequestBody` (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and rejects with **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null or blank. *Side-effect:* republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n2. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Converts `telephone` to E.164 in place (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; a bare number is assumed `+61`, dropping one leading `0`). Rejects with **400** if the result isn't 8\u201315 digits.\n\n3. **ValidateTelephoneLength** \u2014 *validation.* Checks national-number length of the E.164 number: `+61` must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10. Wrong length \u2192 **400**. Other country codes are left alone.\n\n4. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Only if an email is present: rejects with **400** (`InvalidOwnerEmailException`) if it fails the regex, or if its domain is disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); otherwise stores it lower-cased in place. Missing email is untouched.\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 *side-effect.* Rewrites `address` in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, and expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. (Null address left for step 1 to have already rejected.)\n\n6. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 *validation.* Only if a postcode is present: must be 4 digits, and for known cities must fall in range \u2014 Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099. Otherwise **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Unknown city accepts any 4-digit value.\n\n7. **RejectFutureRegistrationDate** \u2014 *validation.* If `registrationDate` is supplied and after `LocalDate.now()`, reject with **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n\n8. **RejectDuplicateIdentity** \u2014 *validation (409).* `govern: [transaction]` starts here. Scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`; rejects with **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`) if the full identity key `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` equals an existing owner's.\n\n9. **RejectDuplicateHousehold** \u2014 *validation (409).* Skipped if `sharesHousehold=true` or no postcode. Otherwise computes `householdId` (from last name + postcode) and rejects with **409** (`DuplicateHouseholdException`) if any existing owner already has it.\n\n10. **RejectCityAtCapacity** \u2014 *validation (409).* Rejects with **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the city (compared case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed) already holds \u2265 50 owners.\n\n11. **RejectDailyLimit** \u2014 *validation (429).* Using the effective registration date rolled onto a business day, rejects with **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`) if \u2265 100 owners are already registered for that day.\n\n12. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity (via `OwnerMapper`), then sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today), rolled forward off weekends to the next Monday (`BusinessDay.roll`).\n\n13. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`: REGION from postcode prefix (20xx\u2192NSW, 30xx\u2192VIC, 40xx\u2192QLD), else by city, else `UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n14. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode` (null if no postcode).\n\n15. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = number of *existing* owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive). Runs before save, so it counts only pre-existing owners.\n\n16. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 *side-effect.* Unless `sharesHousehold=true` or no household: sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the id of the first existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone (soft, non-blocking). Runs before save.\n\n17. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *side-effect.* Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect.* Logs to the `AUDIT` logger: `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`.\n\n19. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect (response).* Maps to `OwnerDto`; applies `HouseholdTier.applyGold` (+2 membership points and recomputed level if the household has \u2265 3 members); sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners are already registered today; responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- Steps 8\u201319 all carry `govern: [transaction]`, so all reads and the save commit as a single transaction at the end of the pipeline.\n- Validation ordering is deliberate: field-presence \u2192 telephone \u2192 email \u2192 address \u2192 postcode \u2192 date \u2192 uniqueness/capacity/rate limits, so cheaper 400s fire before the repository-scanning 409/429 checks.\n- `CheckDigit` and several sibling classes (e.g. `RejectDuplicateEmail`, `RejectDuplicateTelephone`) exist in the package but are **not** wired into this POST pipeline \u2014 duplicate detection here goes solely through the combined `IdentityKey` (step 8) plus the household check (step 9)."
